# What this board does not have, on top of common/kernel.forbidden.

THUNDERBOLT             a Thunderbolt or USB4 port is a PCIe slot on the outside of the case; without this driver it carries USB and DisplayPort and nothing that speaks PCIe
MICROCODE_LATE_LOADING  replacing the microcode of a running CPU, which this image has no blob to do with anyway
X86_MSR                 the model-specific registers as a file to read and write, which is DEVMEM by another name
X86_CPUID               as X86_MSR
EFIVAR_FS               the firmware's own variable store, mounted writable; the stick changes nothing about the machine it is plugged into
RANDOM_TRUST_CPU        a generator inside the CPU cannot be examined, so the kernel mixes RDRAND in without crediting it
RANDOM_TRUST_BOOTLOADER the firmware's seed was chosen by the firmware; mixed in, not credited
PM                      the machine is on or it is off, and runtime power management is what SUSPEND and HIBERNATION are built on
HYPERVISOR_GUEST        this is a kernel for a laptop; it boots in QEMU as a plain emulated PC
VGA_CONSOLE             a machine booted through UEFI is in a graphics mode from the firmware onwards
PCIEPORTBUS             nothing here is hot-plugged, and the controllers are found by enumeration without it
ATA                     the laptop's own SATA or IDE disk; without the driver the kernel never sees it, so nothing on it can be read, written or mounted
BLK_DEV_NVME            the laptop's own NVMe disk, for the same reason
NVME_CORE               the layer BLK_DEV_NVME sits on, named so a driver cannot come back under another menu
MMC                     the laptop's eMMC and its SD card reader, which are a disk and a card this device does not read
SCSI_LOWLEVEL           the SAS, iSCSI, fibre-channel and RAID controllers a disk can be behind; the USB stick is behind none of them

# Faraday (PLAN.md §4.2): no filesystem on a stick is parsed by the kernel.
FAT_FS        a stick's FAT is read by faraday-disk, unprivileged, never by the kernel
VFAT_FS       as FAT_FS
MSDOS_FS      as FAT_FS
EXFAT_FS      a filesystem a stick could carry, and nothing here reads it
NTFS3_FS      as EXFAT_FS
ISO9660_FS    as EXFAT_FS
UDF_FS        as EXFAT_FS
HFSPLUS_FS    as EXFAT_FS

# Faraday (PLAN.md §4.6): USB drivers for storage, HID, video and hubs only.
USB_PRINTER   a printer interface has nothing to bind to here
USB_MON       the USB traffic monitor would show every key a USB keyboard sends
USB_SERIAL    a serial adapter is a way in, not a device this signs with
USB_ACM       as USB_SERIAL

# Faraday (PLAN.md §5.3): no process's memory is ever written to a file.
COREDUMP      a crash would write the app's memory, keys included, to a file

# Upstream hardening (docs/PLANNING.md §16.140), at 96e2144.
IA32_EMULATION          the whole 32-bit system call table; the shell is a static 64-bit binary
MODIFY_LDT_SYSCALL      16-bit segments, for Wine and DOSEMU
X86_16BIT               as MODIFY_LDT_SYSCALL
X86_IOPL_IOPERM         raw I/O port access from a process
DEVPORT                 /dev/port, DEVMEM's sibling for I/O ports
LEGACY_TIOCSTI          pushing characters into a terminal's input queue from a process
HIDRAW                  raw HID reports; input reaches the shell through evdev
USB_HIDDEV              as HIDRAW
VIRTIO                  a PCIe device can present virtio IDs, and VIRTIO_BLK is a block device on a machine whose only storage is the stick
BLK_DEV_SR              binds to any USB device presenting a CD-ROM and parses what it sends
CDROM                   the layer under BLK_DEV_SR, named so it cannot come back under another driver
HID_APPLE               each vendor HID driver binds to IDs any USB device can claim and parses its reports with its own code; HID_GENERIC covers the input
HID_A4TECH              as HID_APPLE
HID_BELKIN              as HID_APPLE
HID_CHERRY              as HID_APPLE
HID_CHICONY             as HID_APPLE
HID_CYPRESS             as HID_APPLE
HID_EZKEY               as HID_APPLE
HID_GYRATION            as HID_APPLE
HID_ITE                 as HID_APPLE
HID_KENSINGTON          as HID_APPLE
HID_LOGITECH            as HID_APPLE
HID_REDRAGON            as HID_APPLE
HID_MICROSOFT           as HID_APPLE
HID_MONTEREY            as HID_APPLE
HID_NTRIG               as HID_APPLE
HID_PANTHERLORD         as HID_APPLE
HID_PETALYNX            as HID_APPLE
HID_SAMSUNG             as HID_APPLE
HID_SONY                as HID_APPLE
HID_SUNPLUS             as HID_APPLE
HID_TOPSEED             as HID_APPLE
HID_PID                 as HID_APPLE
HOTPLUG_PCI             nothing here is hot-plugged
ACPI_TABLE_UPGRADE      replacing ACPI tables at boot, which nothing here needs
EFI_CUSTOM_SSDT_OVERLAYS as ACPI_TABLE_UPGRADE
EFI_RUNTIME_MAP         the EFI memory map in sysfs, which exists for kexec
